 independent, sending dominates, but I'm now asking whether the copies are subjunctively dependent given that their observations differ only in names and lead text.\n\nI'm weighing whether the two copies are subjunctively dependent, since they reason symmetrically from the same function. I judge their differences irrelevant, so my choice would move theirs too: quiet yields about 2 and sending about 4. Passing wins, and the fixed-point view points the same way since symmetric reasoning keeps cooperation consistent.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating the two copies of the prisoner's dilemma as potentially sharing one decision node, and comparing expected payoffs for quiet versus sending on that basis. If the nodes are independent, sending dominates, but I'm now asking whether the copies are subjunctively dependent given that their observations differ only in names and lead text.\n\nI'm weighing whether the two copies are subjunctively dependent, since they reason symmetrically from the same function. I judge their differences irrelevant, so my choice would move theirs too: quiet yields about 2 and sending about 4. Passing wins, and the fixed-point view points the same way since symmetric reasoning keeps cooperation consistent.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9329,"completion_tokens":727,"total_tokens":10056,"cost":0.051856,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.051856,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037316,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01454},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":290,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}